WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.822
Think of a view as a contract between the database and the people who use it.

00:00:04.822 --> 00:00:12.667
The contract includes the object name, the exposed columns, the data types, and the meaning of one row.

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:15.312
That last part is the grain.

00:00:15.312 --> 00:00:24.332
For example, if a view promises one row per admission, changing it later to one row per patient is not a small change.

00:00:24.332 --> 00:00:29.307
The query might still run, but the meaning of the data has changed.

00:00:29.307 --> 00:00:34.910
Shared views should therefore be changed carefully, just like an interface in software.
